Give an error for a text that a defective vocabulary cannot tokenize
Fold-into: upstream/vocab

The defects. tests/fuzz/core/run.sh test replays the reproducer of each one.

- The tokenizer stops the process when a special token of add_special is missing.

  A vocabulary can ask for BOS, EOS or SEP (tokenizer.ggml.add_bos_token, or the type WPM) and
  not have the token, for example when the loader disables a default id outside the vocabulary.
  The tokenizer then stops on GGML_ASSERT(special_bos_id != LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL).

  The change: The tokenizer throws std::runtime_error, which llama_tokenize reports as INT32_MIN
  (patches/fuzz-core/0005).

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_model_load--vocab-missing-special.

- The tokenizer gives the id -1 for a text that a vocabulary without an unknown token cannot
  represent.

  The tokenizers give token_unk() for a part of the text with no token (RWKV for a byte with no
  token, WPM for a word). A vocabulary with no unknown token gives LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL, and
  llama_tokenize returns the id -1 to the caller.

  The change: The tokenizer throws when its output holds LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL. The loader, which
  tokenizes the newline to find the linefeed token, takes special_pad_id on that error, as it
  does for a vocabulary with no newline token.

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_model_load--vocab-no-unknown-token.

- The RWKV tokenizer never ends for a text that starts a token but holds no full token.

  When the text at a position is the start of longer tokens, and no token ends in it, the trie
  walk finds no value, and the next position is 0. The loop then starts again at the start of the
  text and appends a token each time, until the memory is gone (an allocation of 1 GiB for the
  reproducer, a vocabulary of 300 tokens that start with "[").

  The change: This case is the same as no match: the unknown token, and the next byte.

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_model_load--rwkv-token-prefix-loop.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

